# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# client/env.local.example — settings the web app is BUILT with
#
# Local development: copy to client/.env.local and fill it in.
# Production (Render): set them in the dashboard; they are read when
# the app is built, so redeploy after changing one.
#
# EVERYTHING HERE ENDS UP IN THE BROWSER, readable by anyone who opens
# the app. Never put a secret here. Secrets belong on the server
# (server/env.example) and in the password manager.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Nothing here is required: with no .env.local at all the app runs,
# locally (Vite passes /api to the server on port 5000) and on Render
# (the app and the API share one address).

# Only if the API is on a different address from the app. Leave unset
# otherwise: a cross-address API needs CORS and loses the login cookie.
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-api-domain.com

# Address suggestions when adding a centre or kitchen. A PUBLIC Mapbox
# token (starts pk.), restricted to the app's address in the Mapbox
# account. Unset: addresses are typed in full.
# VITE_MAPBOX_PUBLIC_TOKEN=pk.your_public_mapbox_token

# The letterhead on printed delivery and dispatch notes. Defaults to the
# Cape Town warehouse. Separate address lines with |.
# VITE_WAREHOUSE_NAME=Ladles of Love, Cape Town Warehouse
# VITE_WAREHOUSE_ADDRESS=Unit 4, Hewett Park|17 Hewett Ave, Epping|Cape Town, 7460

# The address printed in pallet QR codes. Normally worked out from where
# the app is opened; set it only when that is not the public address
# (for example printing labels from localhost).
# VITE_PUBLIC_APP_ORIGIN=https://your-actual-domain.com
